  "findings": [
    "Both selected toolchains dispatch macOS SystemTime to Unix SystemTime/Timespec; the internal second field is i64 and nanoseconds are normalized.",
    "UNIX_EPOCH is the zero Timespec. Public SystemTime Add calls checked_add and expects success; Unix checked_add uses checked integer seconds and normalized nanosecond carry.",
    "Adding nonnegative Duration below 253402300800 seconds to zero is representable in i64; the existing epoch-only, year-10000-exclusive precondition is preserved.",
    "duration_since delegates to sub_time/sub_timespec, comparing the normalized timestamp and returning the nonnegative Duration difference or an error. Existing Duration-domain restriction and unconstrained error payload remain.",
    "Apple-specific normalization concerns conversion of external pre-epoch timespec values. This does not change epoch addition in the selected domain. Clock reads, arbitrary OS timespec conversion, and Instant are not modeled."
  ]
}
